Hi Jamal,
How many CpGs  and samples you have in your  methylBase object "meth" ? That would affect the memory usage and since you are doing it on two cores, your R session might be duplicating everything in your session so it will increase the memory if you use multiple cores.

You can try to save your "meth" object and start a fresh R session and redo the calculation, this way intermediate objects will be removed from memory and hopefully it won't take as much memory as before.

Best,
Altuna

